The only InfoServer that could ever be put back into a proper condition to
run an OS of any kind other than InfoServer OS is the InfoServer 100.

On the InfoServer 150 we removed the floating point chip and changed the
hardware design of the SCSI interconnect such that the system is not
recognized by OpenVMS as a VAX.

On the InfoServer 1000, we only used a CVAX chip to get some speed of
execution, the unit is definiately not a complete VAX implementation nor
capable of being converted.

The InfoServer 100 conversion would require new ROM's, copies could be made
from a MV3100 model 20.

Why bother, purchase a MV3100 if you need a MicroVAX and if you need a
InfoServer use it as is, or get more than you figured you could by selling
it to someone who could use it. Remember, the InfoServer is in fact still in
some demand by some VAX sites, and some Alpha sites.

rtt





