In article <3840DB34.1A7C@bayarea.net>, Phil Lawson <phil@bayarea.net> writes:
:I've got a VAX 3100 model 10/e that I'm trying to boot, It's got a 25
:pin D type connector, and 3 MMJ connectors. (also power, Ethernet, SCSI
:and expansion connectors)  I don't get anything on console no matter
:what I try, does anyone have the correct cable pinouts, connector, and
:baud rate setting for this box?  Thanks in advance for any help that you
:can provide.

  I will assume this system is a MicroVAX 3100 model 10e series system.

  Look in the OpenVMS FAQ (accessable via http://www.openvms.digital.com/)
  for pointers to various hardware-related websites that may/will be of
  interest here...

  The MMJ pinouts are in the OpenVMS FAQ.

  On at least a few of the MicroVAX 3100 series boxes, the serial console 
  is connected via MMJ port 3 when <break> is enabled via the "S3" switch 
  set upwards (IIRC) -- when S3 set is set downward (IIRC), <break> is 
  disabled and console output goes to MMJ 1.  Both MMJ 1 and MMJ 3 have 
  a habit of displaying the console self-test output...  The DB25 serial 
  line is reserved for use with a modem...

  Also see the FAQ section "VAX5.   Tell me about the system disk size limit 
  on the VAXstation 3100." -- if you have a MicroVAX 3100 model 10e system
  with console PROMs with VMB 6.4 or later, you can use system disks larger 
  than 1.073 GB.  If you have an earlier version, your system disk is and
  must be limited to 1.073 GB or smaller in total capacity...  And see the
  FAQ discussion of just what a <BREAK> signal really generates before you 
  power-cycle a console serial terminal...

