> I have a VAXStation 3100 (Dont know which model - VS42A is all I know)
> which used to have VMS 5.4-3 installed. I say used to because it seems
> to have hardware problems now. The furthest I got was logging in as
> SYSTEM into VMS, and then the only command working was LO (not even SET
> DEFAULT, DIRECTORY etc. all gave %DCL errors "UNRECOGNISED VERB")
> 
> The battery has now gone flat I suspect and it now gives 3 errors on
> the console after POST:
> 
> KA42-A V1.2
> 
> F...E...D...C...B...A...9...8...7...6...5...4...3_..2_..1?..
> 
>  ?  E  0040  0000.0005
>  ?  C  0080  0000.4001
> ??  1  00C0  0000.7004

I think the "E" error is the clock.  When you lost the battery, the
clock lost its setting.  Once you replace the battery and boot VMS and
set the time, this error will go away.

The "C" "error" indicates that you are using a serial terminal as the
console instead of the graphics head.  This is not really an error.  It
is a warning that the serial port used for the console could not be
tested.

The "1" error indicates that you are not connected to a network and the
Ethernet ports are not terminated.

Try the console command "show device".  It should give you a list of
attached disk drives.  Then try booting from these drives "B <drive>"
until you find one that works.  Finally, use the console command "SET
BOOT <drive>" so that drive will be used automagically the next time
that you boot.

Good luck!

