    I don't have my USR command reference handy, but what is your DTR set
to? If DTR/DSR are not high on both ends when the modems are connected,
Win98 may ignore any i/o. USR modems also by default do not have hardware
handshaking enabled. This may not be a problem for the DEC, but will be if
you have Win98 configured to use handshaking and the USR modem is not set to
the same setting. I can't say as to whether or not it uses XON/XOFF and/or
RTS/CTS, RTS/DTR handshaking. On my old USR HST's with my 286 for vt100/ANSI
BBS dialup the settings were:

Receive handshake disabled
Transmit handshake CTS
DTE speed floating
MNP5 compression disabled at&k3 if I remember correctly
DTE to DCE on RTS high

    I can dig out the old HST manual if that doesn't help you.



    Chris




