It sounds like it has been basically nuked.  If you want to run VMS
on it, I can't help much.  If you want to run something unixy, then
I might can help.

> The battery has now gone flat I suspect and it now gives 3 errors on
> the console after POST:

The batteries last a LONG time, or mine do.  I have yet to have one
die.  Check that the battery plug is connected on the motherboard.
Check at the same time that all drive/bus cabling is properly seated.

> KA42-A V1.2

> F...E...D...C...B...A...9...8...7...6...5...4...3_..2_..1?..

>  ?  E  0040  0000.0005
>  ?  C  0080  0000.4001
> ??  1  00C0  0000.7004

> I seem to remember one of these before, but not the Fatal Error on the
> Network Card.

Is the mouse connected?  Plug in a mouse.

Is the ethernet connector terminated?  Plug terminators on both ethernet
lines and see if that goes away.

Is the scsi terminated?  Plug a terminator in on the scsi line.

I am not sure what the last error is, but it might be trying to read
the HD and dying.

> Trying to boot with "b" command gives -ESA0: and then hangs. Does
> anyone know the console commands to help me reconfigure this machine. I
> would like to resurrect it but don't really know how.

OK, it is netbooting.  That usually means the default boot device is
unreadable..... probably nuked HD.

Type from the prom monitor....

>>> show dev

and see what comes back as devices.  It could be the HD is nuked or
erased or unreadble for booting, or something like that.  IFF that
is the case, you need a cd and cdrom drive or tape and tape drive
to boot from, or a way to netboot from another local machine.
If the HD device(s) read OK, then the software is probably nuked.
Reinstall whatever you need to reinstall.  Before reinstalling you
might want to seriously consider a TEST 75 from the prom monitor
to totally low-level reformat any drives.

I netbooted mine from FreeBSD into NetBSD VAX, or booted from cdrom
(DEC RRD42) into Ultrix and then installed NetBSD.  NetBSD works
great on the VS3100 class machines.

http://www.netbsd.org/Ports/vax/  for starters.

