> 
> KA42-A V1.2
> 
> F...E...D...C...B...A...9...8...7...6...5...4...3_..2_..1?..
> 
>  ?  E  0040  0000.0005

This is probably the battery error.

>  ?  C  0080  0000.4001

TEST C is the DZ device, which is the serial ports, kbd and mouse.  Are
you using a graphics console, or a VT terminal?

> ??  1  00C0  0000.7004

TEST 1 is the NI device, which is the Ethernet.  Make sure that it is
terminated.

> Trying to boot with "b" command gives -ESA0: and then hangs. Does

It is trying to net boot (ESA0) which is the default after the battery
goes dead.

You need to

>>> set boot dka0

(or whichever device the OS is on.

For more information try:

>>> TEST 0

which will do a more extensive self test.

-mikeu



