e40@home.com wrote:
> 
> Hello -
> 
> I have run short of tapes, and I'm trying to figure out
> what kind to use in my TZ87 drives.  The pool of working
> tapes are DLT CompacTape III's. (Digital logo on them)
> The new ones we have tried are Fujifilm DLTtape III [xt]'s.
> But I get parity errors when trying to initialize them.
> I have tried initializing on both platforms..(VMS and
> DECunix, both have the TZ87 drive)

You want the non-XT version of the DLT III.  The "XT" means extended
tape length, and I'm under the impression that the TZ87 transport
doesn't deal with the skinnier longer tapes.

I buy my non-XT DLT III's from Microwarehouse (www.warehouse.com),
their part number for the Sony DLT III is ME7857.  These work just
fine in my TZ877 (the autochanger version of the TZ87.)

Tim.



