Keith,

MCHK670 is a fatal processor machine check (error detected by the CPU). Error
code 0x94 is a primary Icache data fill parity error. This indicates that data
with a parity error was received from Bcache or memory while performing an
Icache fill. If you could post or email the entire MCHK670 entry out of the
binary.errlog I could probably tell you more. Specifically, you need to look at
these registers:

   BIU_STAT
   FILL_ADDR
   FILL_SYNDROME
   BC_TAG

The faulty FRU is a CPU card if BC_TAG<0> = 1
The faulty FRU is a memory module (SIMM) if BC_TAG<0> = 0

You performed an SRM firmware update from the console using the v5.5 firmware CD
before trying to install TRU64 UNIX v5.0, right? Followed all the installation
prerequisites?

--> Jay


