In article <60D1BEC57BB67429.874CC7445BF08220.D96C6E8939AA311C@lp.airnews.net>, "Dizzy" <jdisnard@hotmail.com> writes:
..
:WHAT VIDEO CARD IS BEST FOR ALPHA???????
..

  That depends on what you want to do, on what you want to pay, and on
  what operating system you want to use...  (None of which should come 
  as a particular surprise, of course...)

  The Matrox Millenium is not supported by all operating system platforms 
  that run on OpenVMS Alpha -- since this discussion is cross-posted over
  to the OpenVMS newsgroup, I'll cover OpenVMS.  AFAIK, OpenVMS and Tru64
  UNIX do not support any of the various Matrox cards...

  PowerStorm 3D30 and PowerStorm 4D20 are probably the fastest 2D cards 
  around, if you can get your hands on one -- OpenVMS, Tru64 UNIX, and 
  Windows NT Alpha all support these cards.  Also available is the ELSA 
  GLoria Synergy card, with support on OpenVMS covered in the OpenVMS FAQ.

  There are certainly older cards around that are supported by one or more 
  of the operating systems.  ATI Mach64 CX and GX, S3 Trio64, S3 Trio64V, 
  and the ZLXp series are available choices for OpenVMS.  The upper-end 
  PowerStorm series (the 40 and up) are generally not supported by OpenVMS, 
  but are likely available on Tru64 UNIX and (probably) NT.  (I don't follow 
  the Tru64 UNIX and NT device support announcements...)

  OpenVMS is adding support for the PowerStorm 300 and PowerStorm 350 for
  later this year...

  The OpenVMS, Open3D, and DECwindows SPDs are generally a good source
  for the list of supported graphics controller widgets...

  Me?  I happen to like the PowerStorm 3D30 and the PowerStorm 4D20...

 --------------------------- pure personal opinion ---------------------------
   Hoff (Stephen) Hoffman   OpenVMS Engineering   hoffman#xdelta.zko.dec.com




