Joshua Lutz (josh@prowireless.com) wrote:
: Hi, Stu:
: 
: I'm not certain, that I understand you correctly. If I have a wide scsi
: controller (in my case a DEC 3100 rackmount with SCA drivebays) and I have
: one narrow SCSI CD ROM drive (as normally configured by DEC), then I will
: still achieve the maximum throughput to the SCA drives that they can
: handle? - ie the presence of the narrow SCSI CD doesn't choke the hard drive
: throughput in any way?

That's exactly right.

The controller and the drive negotiate at initialization time to determine how
fast each will go.  Each drive is individually negotiated with to determine
its bus speed.

However, note that a slow device may tend to tie up the bus for longer periods
of time, hence may tend to slow down faster devices, if for no other reason
than the fast device can't get on the bus until the slower device is finished.

