In response to your questions...

I am not completely familiar with the main logic board in the DECpc XL
466D2.  It is similar to the one used in the later Celebris XL: same
layout, same chipsets, etc.  But here's my best guess, given the
relative age of the board and its BIOS:

1. The EIDE BIOS limit is 524MB, the original size limit for IDE
drives.
2. A 1GB SCSI drive is a cinch.  Anything above 1GB depends mostly on
the BIOS, and I haven't checked.
3. Memory must be fast page mode with parity bit, 70 ns. or faster.

None of the DEC BIOS upgrades for this board will raise the limits.

Suggestion to modernize the system, if you are willing and able to
take on a little work:

Replace the main logic board with a Celebris XL board, and replace the
processor card with a Pentium-class card.  The BIOS limits would be
raised considerably, to 8GB for EIDE and I don't know how big for
SCSI, but a lot bigger.

I have kits to upgrade a DECpc XL to a Celebris XL, and also memory.

