Al Losada wrote:
> 
> Very new to DEC. I have an Alpha 255 and cannot login. Root or any other
> login does not work. I figure that I need to boot off the CD to break
> security but need some help doing so. Any ideas?

Well, you have to get it to halt at first, ie. turn off the power and
pray that nothing in the filesystem gets damaged.

Then boot it again and press <Ctrl> + <c> (or <Ctrl + <p>). This will
prevent it from booting and leave you at the boot-prompt.

See if auto_action is set to boot. If it is then set it to halt (set
auto_action halt) so the machine won't boot by itself when you turn on
power. When everything works again you can set it back (set auto_action
boot).

If you halted the boot too early, you might need to do a init (init), or
you can just turn off the power and turn it on again. Then the machine
should stop by itself at the boot-prompt.

Now boot it in single-user (boot -fl s). After a while you'll get your
prompt. Then you have to mount the filesystems in read/write mode (the
only present is the root filesystem, and it's in read only mode).

You can either just remount the root file system (mount -u -w /), or
mount'em all (bcheckrc). The last thing will also give you access to vi
and other nice tools.


Then do a passwd to thange the root password.


If it asks for the old password, you're running C2, and you need to do
more stuff to change the password.


When done do a shutdown -r now, and when it's up again... test it.



l8r/Jspr



