Hi,
Maybe, there is some nonstandard config written into the NIC's NVRAM,
so you should type that exact parameters in isacfg (IRQ, memory base,
memory size, IO port, etc.).
How you can see them? There must be some SRM command to change DE205
NVRAM contents. Maybe, it's called nicsetup, or something like this.
Or maybe there is some add_de205 switches to write a config to NVRAM.
(I haven't got such an Alpha for now, so I can only remember. But I
really did it on AS250 two or three years ago). Anyway, you can
install the card into any PC and run a PC version of nicsetup which is
available at Digital's web site. (The name of the program may be
changed). There are some docs too. Also, the card has two jumpers
(blue), they must be removed normally. Their purpose is to set a
pre-wired config, if there is an ISA conflict, preventing you from
running nicsetup. Also note that you must power-cycle the machine for
DE205 to re-read its NVRAM. And finally, not all possible values are
right for Alpha, so it's better to set values below (memlen 10000
stands for 64K).
I hope, it will help.
Regards,
Eugene.




