I'm also in the process of trying to resurrect one of my BA23's, but with a PDP1183
boardset. The backplane scheme is about the same as for your uVAX.

The 3 right slots (as viewed from the rear) are used for your CPU/mem. The cpu
going to the rightmost slot, and 2 mem boards to its left (you do have the ribbon
jumpering the mem-cpu, right?)

> It has a Microvax II CPU board, 8 MB ram board, M7555, M7516, and M7546. It
> also has a lot of Grant cards.
>

With only one mem board, you can use either a quad or dual board in slot 3 but a
dual MUST be mounted in the upper half. Leave the lower half empty, no grant card.
Slots 4 on up follow a serpentine priority pattern starting at top of 4 down, up
thru 5 and so on. Use a grant card in any of these slots where only one dual is
installed, unless it is the last board.

The RQDX3 (M7555) is generally placed last. But if you experience tape problems
I've seen that placing the tape controller at the end may sometimes help.

>
> Did I just blow the CPU board, if so, does anyone know what I can do to
> resurect it?
>

If indeed your CPU is blown, I have a KA630 here just collecting dust which you are
welcome to. Im nearby in the Houston area, so contact me at the lower address.
If you need I can fax you the backplane diagram from my manual.


