>(then the hard drive failed the day i brought it home, and i've been trying
>to get it to do something ever since!!)

Are you sure you have the correct file name in /tftpboot/mop?  My 
/tftpboot/mop looks like:

lrwxrwxrwx   1 root root   11 Oct 31 16:24 08002b0db20f.SYS -> current.sys
lrwxrwxrwx   1 root root   45 Oct 31 16:37 current.sys -> /..../vmlinux.SYS

Note that you must have the file <VAX-ether-addr-in-lower-case>.SYS and
it must be in /tftpboot/mop (unless you modify mopd).

I seem to remember mopd looping on me.  It _may_ have been because the file
name wasn't right.

Try running strace on mopd.

Later,
Kenn




