DECtalk was a circa-mid-80's voice synthesizer that could convert ASCII text
to one of your choice of eight voices. DECtalk morphed into a software-based
solution and was one of the numerous technologies sold off by DEC.

DECtalk provided the voice in the movie "Short Circuit." It is unknown
whether a Bob Palmer or Eckhard Pfeiffer voice was ever developed for the
product.

charlie matco





