Stepanov wrote:

> Hello.
>
> I have a question.
> I need some device that make connection between PDP-11 and PC bus ( bus
> of PDP11 and EISA).
> Where I can find it or may be there are some example, how to do such
> kind of devices.
> Thanks for any advice.

     I know of several ways of doing this, none "directly".  First,
assuming there are two physical machines, they can be connected via serial
ports and communication through Kermit (slow).  Second, they can be
connected via Ethernet and communication through TCP/IP (faster).  Third,
you can "embed" the PDP-11 inside the PC using one of several
PDP-11 emulation programs, so your "PDP-11" will be directly using the PC's
disk.  Fourth, I believe there are PCs that plug into the Q-bus, so you can
put a PC "inside" the PDP-11.  Don't know what they do about the bus, but I
presume that the PC can use the Q-bus ...

     I have experience with the first three methods.

Bob Schor






