Frank Turner <snowman@ctel.net> wrote:
> Hi.
> I just got a DECstation 2100 ans was hoping to get some help setting it
> up.

Sure, what do you need to know?

> Will it run Linux?

No.  There is a DECstation linux port, but it is not anywhere much, yet.
The NetBSD and OpenBSD ports are mature and entirely usable, now.

> I was told that there were VMS images available for this machine.
> Is that true?

No.  VMS will not run on this hardware, AFIK, only VAX hardware.

> Any HOW-TO's would be appreciated.

Look at http://www.netbsd.org/Ports/pmax for starters.

The NetBSD-1.4.1 runs well on my machines.

Look at http://www.openbsd.org/pmax.html for the OpenBSD version.

The machine is usually netbooted via the ethernet and then ftp installed.
This requires a local unix boot server machine of some sort (I used an
old FreeBSD x86ish box), with an anonymous ftp login.  It can be booted
from Ultrix.

Check the internal memory installed.  16mb was common, and full up is
24mb.  The usual tiny RZ23 drives are too small to be of much use these
days.  A pair or triplet of RZ25 drives makes a comfy little box, or
a pair or triplet of RZ24 drives make for a tight, but usable box.
Normal drive trays would handle two drives, but some had an internal
floppy drive, which, when removed will allow 3 internal drives.
The floppy is mostly useless.

> Thanks!
> -Frank

Good Luck, and enjoy your OT unix box!

Bob




