camillei@my-deja.com wrote:
> Hi,

> I have a couple of DEC SCSI drives that I am interested in buying but I have
> no idea what the capacities are. The drive models are 3100D and 3200D. Any
> info or URLs would be greatly appreciated.

Those sound like DEC RZ23 and RZ24 drives.  100 and 200 mb each, scsi,
old and slow, but useful in apples or as temp drive space.  I would not
give over a couple of bucks each for them.  More than that and you are
being taken for a song.  They are equivalent to the old Conner CP-3100 and
CP-3200 scsi drives, but with DEC roms.  Look on the tops of them for a
label that should say something like RZ23 or RZ24.   There are equivalent
drives of about the same size with RZ labels on them that will have an
L designation, and are slightly bigger.

Drive/jumpering info can be found on http://theref.aquascape.com/theref.html 

The RZ23 has 776C 8H 33S.

The RZ24 has 1366C (or maybe 1372C) 8H 38S.

Good Luck....

Bob



