M. Eric Christy <christy@jlab.org> wrote:

> I have a pc164 based machine running SRM and I am trying to install a 
> de205 ethernet card.  I've tried to use isacfg to configure the slot 
> but the card never shows up when doing 'show dev'.  Any ideas.  A brief 
> step by step would be appreciated by someone who has done this before.

There is SRM-command add_de205 , which does the right isacfg. (See:
>>> more add_de205). First you may need to clear ISA config tables by:
>>> isacfg -init  

In case your SRM doesn't have add_de205 (I don't see it in help), my
164SX SRM 5.5-1 has:

>>> more add_de205
isacfg -slot 1 -dev 0 -mk -handle DE200-LE -irq0 5 -iobase0 300 -membase0
d0000 -memlen0 10000 -etyp 1 -enadev 1      (copied by hand from display)

regards
        Osmo Kujala



