Along with a friend of mine, he and I transposed the manufacture of the
JENSEN product, from the UK to North America, specifically here in Canada,
where all Alpha's were made at one time. The JENSEN was the DEC 2000 aka the
DECpc AXP 150 and was a seed unit for Alpha and Windows NT. It unfortunately
had a longer than intended lifetime as the MORGAN (the was no Triumph) was
delayed again and again. Ultimately, the MORGAN was cancelled. The
cancelation was based strictly on technical reasons, the sole guy spinning
the specialized PAL's for the MORGAN was in fact working for a
sub-contractor and he got a better job offer and the contractor could not
deliver the final spin of silicon. This engineering nightmare caused all
furture design to be moved to the US, and thus the naming convention
followed that of north Amercan cars such as MUSTANG, etc...

I repeat, there was no Triumph and in fact the machine canceled was the
MORGAN and that for sound technical reasons, not politics.

