I run two external DLT4000 on a cheap Symbios SYM8751SP in a 433au
( OS is 4.0D ). A cheap NCR810 clone will work too. They both use the 
same driver which was originally written for a DEC labeled NCR810 clone.
I would avoid the Tekram, better get the original Symbios card. 
The Tekram has a slightly different hardware design as the Symbios 
card and because the DEC driver are for a Symbios reference design, 
it's possible that the Tekram card causes problems. The Symbios 
card is cheaper too (65$ at http://www.centrix-intl.com/). 

