Norbert Schmal wrote:
> Does anyone know, how to prevent printing of the
> summary sheet after power-on a DEC LN03
> Laser printer ?

On the LN03 and LN03-PLUS printer, there are 2 packs of dip switches in the
back. However, neither have any settings for production of status page at power-on.

To generate a summary sheet, you you press the [T] button in the back of the
printer (towards the lower right, lokking at the printer from the front).

There is a note which specifies that the summary sheet can be printed "on
request" while loading new fonts to the printer.

Perhaps you have an LN03-R postscript printer.



