In article <EUUS3.24473$0t5.149196@news.chello.at>,
  Wolfgang Rupp <rupp@chello.at> wrote:
> The battery in my VAXstation 3100M38 is nearly dead. Since the battery
> is simply plugged into the maimboard, it should not be a problem to
> change it. Can someone please specify the voltage needed? I assume a
> few NiCADs soldered together should do...

My experience of soldering Nicads is that it has always resulted in
premature failure of one of the cells. Do it quickly, with low melting
temperature solder if possible. Alternatively, you may be able to buy a
pack of 3 cells as replacements for mobile or cordless telephones
(they're quite cheap on the electronics surplus market here in the UK).
Check the voltage, though -- not eveything that looks like a single
cell really is!

Chris


