This goes back to one of the root problems with Alpha. According to the
original business plan for Alpha (based on "highly classified" 1991
documents), DEC planned to sell millions and millions of Alpha chips per
year, thus making lots of dinero. Alas, nowhere in the business plan was
anything mentioned about the OS that would run on these chips. When NT
finally shipped, DEC was dumb enough to negotiate a really lousy deal (the
Allliance for Enterprise Computing) with Microsoft. The rest is history.





