VMS will reset a bus and thus the SDTR and WDTR negotiations start
from narrow/asynch. However if you're using a VMS prior to 7.1
there was rework of SDTR, and WDTR was completely missing,
which could have missed something. You'd certainly need a wide
to narrow adaptor (dwzza?) if you want anything to work, and the
terminator and bus had better be up to snuff. It's easy to get
away with passive terminators & long busses if your disks are old
slow ones.

Also there were some issues with some Seagate disks misimplementations
of tagged queueing at one time. You might have to disable tagged
queueing (dque bit) on the drive. I just don't recall the
drives that were involved, and never did pay much attention to
the models. I am using an ST15150WC on a 3000-300LX as I write
this and it does work btw.

