> yup it's a micropolis drive allright, i guess this means that the machine will just boot
> up by fluke every now and again. i'll try the st st251 and play with the jumpers for a
> while as the primary drive. will any old mfm drive work on it if it's under a gig and i
> know the drive specs to tell the formatter?


1GB is a non-issue for an MFM drive.  As far as I know, the highest
capacity MFM drive made was the Maxtor 2190 at 160MB.  The VS2000 will
recognize this drive as a RD54.

The ST251 should be recognized as an RD32.

For an unrecognized drive, TESET 70 will prompt for the various
parameters.  One non-obvious parameter is the Media ID.  This is the
MSCP ID.  I think it is only important if you MSCP serve the drive.

The ID for an RD54 is 627327030.

Good luck!

