The MicroVAX II could support up to 3 CPU boards in the first 3 slots.  This
wouldn't have left any slots open for memory though!  This would leave each
CPU limited to the 1 MB of memory that was on the CPU board.  Even if you
put two CPUs in and used the remaining slot for memory, the second CPU
couldn't connect to that memory and would be limited to its private 1 MB.  I
don't know if VAXeln supported multiple CPUs but it certainly wouldn't
surprise me if it did.


