In comp.sys.dec James Paton <jamesp@rcp.co.uk> wrote:
> I don't have much VMS knowledge but from the HELP I've
> done all the stuff like AUTOCONFIGURE ALL from SYSGEN
> and then mounting the new disk.

  Unless you're doing a minimum startup, the system startup scripts
should do the autoconfigure for you. Try rebooting and not doing
the autoconfigure and see if the disk shows up as "Online".

> SHO DEV then displays the 2nd disk, but as MOUNT ALLOC
> whereas DKA300 is MOUNT

  That's because it's allocated to your process because you didn't say
/SYSTEM on the MOUNT command.

> My problem is that if I reset the box and do SHO DEV again
> it's forgotten I have the new disk...
>
> What commands do I need to run to get it to remember the
> settings/new disk ?

  Edit SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM and stick the MOUNT/SYSTEM command
in there. If anyone else is reading this and has a VMS V5 VAX, that file
used to be called SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_V5.COM.

