Pete Humble wrote:
> 
> Thanks for posting that.
> 
> It has reminded me of a question:
> I know what some of the prefixes to module numbers mean:
> G(reen), M(agenta), W(hite)
> 
> Does anyone know what these stand for?

I can't tell you "officially", but I'll tell you what they mean
in my mind :-).

> A?

Analog.  (At least to my mind!  Nearly all instrumentation-intended
A/D and D/A converters start with A).

>  H?

The universal designator for a "module" which is not
just a PCB, but also a mechanical assembly.  Cab kits, power supplies,
etc.  (Though note that some cab kits do have a M number.)

>  L?

"Large"?.  Certainly the L-series boards that I first encountered -
those in 11/750's - are larger than even a hex-height "standard"
module.

Tim.



