> Not offical DEC at all:

	???

> 'A' = Amber (normally used for _A_nalogue parts).

	Used for _a_nalog cards (muxes, a/d, d/a/ amps sold by Digital.

> 'H' = Hardware, used originally for racks, PSUs, etc. For some reason
>       core planes were classed here

	Historically 'core' came in a bolt in box.  Plug in planes
	were later...

	L:	Can't recall.

> Others :
 
> 'B' = Blue

	fast, discrete, transistor logic.  (faster than 'R', qv)

> 'R' = Red

	discrete transistor logic.  Slower than 'B'.

> 'S' = Scarlet (?). This was the same colour as 'R' and the modules were
> similar as well

	discrete transistor logic.  Faster than R slower than B.

> 'K' = blacK

	Willfully slowed, for noise immunity, in industrial applications.
	Mostly IC, if i recall.

	None of the above (save 'M') are, technically, QBus or Unibus, tho
	the connectors were 'the same' (more or less...)

